icantly improves perf."}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2022-01-20T22:34:45Z","updated_at":"2023-12-16T00:19:23Z","closed_at":"2023-12-01T07:54:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Version\r\n3.2.27\r\n\r\n### Reproduction link\r\n[github.com](https://github.com/SquidEpps/vue-ssr-computed)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n```sh\r\nyarn\r\n\r\nnode index.js\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What is expected?\r\nComputed value is updated and html renders with correct message.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n<div>hello world</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What is actually happening?\r\nComputed value is not updated and an empty div is rendered.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n<div></div>\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\nI'm not sure if this a bug or is it me misusing computed in SSR context, but such an app architecture as in my reproduction demo seems to me completely valid and should work.\r\n\r\nThere is a computed value in a component which is based on part of app's state. No value serves as indication of the need to fetch data. Normally this should happen either during SSR or on the client if the state (or its part) was not hydrated. Async setup function allows to wait for data to be fetched which should trigger an update of state and computed value.\r\n\r\nThis acually worked in 3.2.26. New behavior was possibly introduced in commit [f4f0966](https://github.com/vuejs/core/commit/f4f0966b33863ac0fca6a20cf9e8ddfbb311ae87)\r\n\r\n<!-- generated by vue-issues. DO NOT REMOVE -->","closed_by":{"login":"yyx990803","id":499550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTU1MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/499550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yyx990803","html_url":"https://github.com/yyx990803",